  "slug": "kemoket",
  "name": "Kemoket",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Kemoket (けもケット) is a kemono-themed dōjinshi fair and the largest kemono event in Japan, held twice a year in the Kanto and Kansai regions. The first was held May 3, 2012, in Tokyo, followed by the first Kansai edition in Osaka in September 2012, and the main organizer is Gallone (がろーね). The \"circles\" are the dōjinshi groups that attend as vendors, and the number of circles has grown from 114 to several hundred. A New Year edition, Shinshun Kemoket, has also been held in Kawaguchi since 2015. The fair is held in venues such as the Tokyo Trade Center, the Osanbashi Yokohama Hall and Kyocera Dome Osaka.",
